uilding with AI-accelerated planning\nL308: \nL309: June 2026 Responsibility & Safety\nL310: \nL311: cite99†Learn more L312: \nL313: cite100†Image†lh3.googleusercontent.com L314: \nL315: 1 cite101†Page 2 cite102†Page 3 … cite103†Page 19 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn647view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 943\nL0: [Button: ]\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search]\nL3: \nL4: `/`\nL5: \nL6:   * English\nL7:   * Deutsch\nL8:   * Español – América Latina\nL9:   * Français\nL10:   * Indonesia\nL11:   * Italiano\nL12:   * Polski\nL13:   * Português – Brasil\nL14:   * Shqip\nL15:   * Tiếng Việt\nL16:   * Türkçe\nL17:   * Русский\nL18:   * עברית\nL19:   * العربيّة\nL20:   * فارسی\nL21:   * हिंदी\nL22:   * বাংলা\nL23:   * ภาษาไทย\nL24:   * 中文 – 简体\nL25:   * 中文 – 繁體\nL26:   * 日本語\nL27:   * 한국어\nL28: cite0†Get API key†aistudio.google.com cite1†Cookbook†github.com cite2†Community†discuss.ai.google.dev Sign in\nL29: \nL30: cite3†Docs cite4†API reference L31: \nL32: [Input: Filter]\nL33: \nL34: [Button: ]\nL35: \nL36:   * Get started\nL37: \nL38:   * Models\nL39:   * Robotics\nL40: \nL41:   * Core capabilities\nL42: \nL43:   * Image\nL44: \nL45:   * Video\nL46: \nL47:   * Speech and audio\nL48: \nL49:   * Thinking\nL50: \nL51:   * Agents\nL52: \nL53:   * Tools\nL54: \nL55:   * Live API\nL56: \nL57:   * Get started\nL58: \nL59:   * Optimization\nL60: \nL61:   * Guides\nL62: \nL63:   * File input\nL64: \nL65:   * Logs and datasets\nL66: \nL67:   * Safety\nL68: \nL69:   * Frameworks\nL70: \nL71:   * Resources\nL72: \nL73:   * Migration\nL74: \nL75:   * cite5†Status†aistudio.google.com L76:   * Google AI Studio\nL77: \nL78:   * Google Cloud Platform\nL79: \nL80:   * Policies\nL81: \nL82: [Button: Send feedback ]\nL83: # Release notes\nL84: \nL85: This page documents updates to the Gemini API.\nL86: \nL87: ## September 3, 2026\nL88: \nL89:   * Lyria 3.5 in public preview: Released the next generation of Google's music generation model:\nL90: \nL91:     * cite6†`lyria-3.5` : Full-length song generation with improved musical coherence, natural vocals, and fine-grained duration and structural control.\nL92: \nL93: The model supports text and image inputs and generates high-fidelity 44.1 kHz stereo audio. See the cite7†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL94: ## September 2, 2026\nL95: \nL96:   * Gemini 3.8 Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-3.8-flash`, our most intelligent Flash model, engineered for long-horizon software engineering, autonomous agents, and complex enterprise workflows.\nL97: \nL98: To get started, see the cite8†Gemini 3.8 Flash model page and the cite9†Latest model guide .\nL99: ## September 1, 2026\nL100: \nL101:   * Agentic video understanding: Released agentic video understanding for Gemini 3.7 Flash, 3.6 Flash, and 3.5 Flash-Lite across the Interactions and GenerateContent APIs. The model dynamically navigates video timelines, requesting transcripts, frames, or audio tracks on demand. This approach uses up to 88% fewer tokens for long-form content compared to static processing.\nL102: \nL103: To get started, see the cite10†Agentic video understanding guide.\nL104: ## August 27, 2026\nL105: \nL106:   * Gemini Omni Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-omni-1.1-flash`, the GA version of our fast, conversational video generation and editing model. This release includes significant new capabilities:\nL107:     * Video extension: Seamlessly extend existing videos by generating continuations at the end of a clip using the `extend` task or directly with a prompt.\nL108:     * Interpolation (first + last frame): Generate a video transitioning between two images using the `image_to_video` task with up to 2 images.\nL109:     * Resolution control: New `resolution` parameter in `video_config` supports `360p`, `720p` (default), `1080p`, and `4k` outputs. 1080p and 4K outputs are generated using upscaling.\nL110: The existing `gemini-omni-flash-preview` endpoint will be deprecated on September 30, 2026.\nL111: \nL112: To get started, see the cite11†Gemini Omni Flash model page and the cite12†omni guide .\nL113: ## August 26, 2026\nL114: \nL115:   * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe generally available (GA): Released two dedicated speech-to-text models based on Gemini's audio understanding:\nL116:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`): High-accuracy, low-latency non-streaming speech-to-text with utterance-based language detection across 85+ languages, speaker diarization, word-level timestamps, and custom vocabulary biasing (up to 1,000 terms).\nL117:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe Live (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`): Low-latency, bidirectional streaming speech-to-text over WebSockets using the Live API, supporting interim and finalized transcription events, Smart transcription mode, and multiple Voice Activity Detection (VAD) strategies.\nL118: To get started, see the cite13†Audio transcription guide , the cite14†Live transcription guide , and the cite15†Gemini 3.5 Transcribe model page .\nL119: ## August 13, 2026\nL120: \nL121:   * Gemini 3.7 Flash generally available (GA): Released our most intelligent workhorse model yet for coding and agents:\nL122: \nL123:     * Gemini 3.7 Flash (`gemini-3.7-flash`): Substantial improvements across software engineering, web development, and agentic workflows, available at an introductory price through December 31, 2026.\nL124: \nL125: To get started, see the cite16†Gemini 3.7 Flash model page and the cite9†Latest model guide .\nL126: ## July 30, 2026\nL127: \nL128:   * Gemini Robotics ER 2 in public preview: Released two new embodied reasoning model endpoints for robotics:\nL129: \nL130:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-preview`: Advanced spatial reasoning, agentic code execution, multi-step tool orchestration, video moment finding, progress classification, and multi-robot coordination.\nL131:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-streaming-preview`: Optimized for real-time text streaming using the Live API, enabling low-latency robot agents with bidirectional audio and video input.\nL132: Both model endpoints accept text, image, video, and audio inputs and support function calling with blocking behavior for physical robot actions. To get started, see the cite17†Gemini Robotics ER overview . For real-time streaming use cases, see cite18†Robotics with streaming .\nL133: \nL134:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` model will be cite19†shut down on August 31, 2026.\nL135: ## July 21, 2026\nL136: \nL137:   * Gemini 3.6 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite generally available (GA): Released stable, production-ready versions of our latest 3.x Flash models:\nL138:     * Gemini 3.6 Flash (`gemini-3.6-flash`): Features improved token efficiency and code/agentic planning capabilities at a lower price point than 3.5 Flash, resolving developer feedback around output verbosity.\nL139:     * Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`): Offers a low-latency, highly cost-effective subagent option designed for high-volume automation.\nL140: \nL141: To learn more, see the cite9†Latest Gemini model guide.\nL142:   * Deprecated parameters: The sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are now deprecated. See the cite20†Latest Gemini Model for details.\nL143: ## July 6, 2026\nL144: \n"
